+### FAQ
+
+#### What are the best open source AI tools for lawyers in 2026?
+The strongest legal-specific GitHub repos in this list are `LexNLP`, `ContraxSuite`, `OpenNyAI`, `LegalBench`, and `CUAD`. In practice, most serious legal systems also need supporting open-source infrastructure such as `Unstructured`, `Docling`, `Haystack`, `LlamaIndex`, `Qdrant`, and `Ollama`.
+
+#### Are there any truly self-hosted AI tools for lawyers on GitHub?
+Yes, but the legal-specific category is still small. The most realistic self-hosted legal stack combines public GitHub repos for OCR, parsing, retrieval, vector search, local model serving, transcription, and workflow automation rather than depending on a single all-in-one legal AI repository.
+
+#### Which open source tools are best for contract review and clause extraction?
+Start with `LexNLP`, `ContraxSuite`, and `CUAD` for contract-focused work. Pair them with `Unstructured` or `Docling` for ingestion, then use `Haystack`, `LangChain`, or `LlamaIndex` plus a vector database for retrieval and grounded analysis.
+
+#### Which GitHub repos help lawyers process scanned PDFs and court filings?
+`OCRmyPDF`, `Tesseract`, `PaddleOCR`, `Apache Tika`, `Unstructured`, and `Docling` are the strongest open-source options in this list for turning scanned or messy files into searchable, structured inputs for legal review.
+
+#### What is the best open source legal AI stack for private law firm deployment?
+A practical private stack is `OCRmyPDF` or `PaddleOCR` for scans, `Unstructured` or `Docling` for parsing, `Haystack` or `LlamaIndex` for retrieval logic, `Qdrant` or `Weaviate` for storage, and `Ollama`, `vLLM`, `TGI`, or `LocalAI` for self-hosted inference.
+
+#### Are there enough public GitHub repositories dedicated only to legal AI?
+Not yet. That is the main gap this repository documents honestly. The legal-native open-source niche is still much smaller than the general open-source AI ecosystem, so lawyers usually assemble domain workflows from a mix of legal-specific repos and broader open infrastructure.
